hadiths[196]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20338","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Mansur from Hilal ibn Yasaf from Rabi ibn Umaylah from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not name your boy Aflah nor Najih nor Yasar nor Rabah, for if you say: Is he there, or is so-and-so there, they will say: No."
"20339","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us from a shaykh of Banu Qushayr, Rawh said: He said: I heard Sawadah al-Qushayri, and he was their imam, he said: I heard Samurah ibn Jundub preaching, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the call of Bilal nor this whiteness deceive you until the dawn bursts or the dawn rises."
"20340","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah informed us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Mabad ibn Khalid narrating from Zayd ibn Uqbah from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and: Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming."
"20341","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two pauses in his prayer. And Imran ibn Husayn said: I do not remember them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they wrote about that to Ubayy ibn Kab asking him about it, and Ubayy wrote that Samurah had remembered correctly."
"20342","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Said narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is Asr. Ibn Jafar said: He was asked about the middle prayer."
"20343","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, and Yazid said: Said informed us, and Bahz, Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah ibn Jundub from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Every boy is pledged for his aqiqah, slaughtered for him on his seventh day. And Bahz said in his hadith: And blood is smeared and he is named therein and shaved, Yazid said: His head."
"20344","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, and Bahz, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from al-Hasan from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umra is permissible for its people. Ibn Jafar said in his hadith: For its people, or inheritance for its people."
"20345","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with doubt in it in the book of sales, and he said: From Uqbah or Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whichever woman two guardians marry off, she belongs to the first of them, and whoever sells a sale to two men, it belongs to the first of them."
"20346","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, they said: Said narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah ibn Jundub from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The hand is liable for what it takes until it renders it. And Ibn Bishr said: Until it renders."
"20347","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, and Yazid, and Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Qudamah ibn Wabarah a man of Banu Ujayf narrated to me from Samurah ibn Jundub from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever leaves a Friday without excuse, let him give a dinar in charity, and if he does not find, then half a dinar."
"20348","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of the house has more right to the house than another."
"20349","Bahz and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah, Abd al-Samad said: Qatadah narrated to me, from al-Hasan from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution, then with it and excellent, and whoever bathes, that is better. Abd al-Samad said in his hadith: Qatadah narrated to us."
"20350","Bahz and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah, Abd al-Samad said: Qatadah narrated to me, from al-Hasan from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two guardians marry a woman, she belongs to the first of them, and when a sale is sold to two men, it belongs to the first of them."
"20351","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from al-Hasan from Samurah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard the prayers. Affan said: The prayer, and the middle prayer. And he named it for us: It is only the Asr prayer."
"20352","Bahz narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from al-Hasan from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Hunayn on a rainy day: Prayer in the dwellings."
"20353","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, he said: And a man narrated to me, he said: I heard Samurah preaching upon the minbar of Basra, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woman was created from a rib, and if you wish to straighten the rib you will break it, so deal gently with her and you will live with her."
"20354","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Awf narrated to us from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, Samurah ibn Jundub al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: Among what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to his companions was: Has any of you seen a dream? He said: Whoever Allah willed to narrate would narrate to him. He said: And he said to us one morning: Two comers came to me tonight and roused me, and they said to me: Proceed, and I proceeded with them. We came upon a man lying down with another standing over him with a rock, striking his head with the rock, crushing his head with it, and the stone rolled here, and he followed the stone to take it, and he did not return to him until his head became sound as it was, then he returned to him and did to him as he did the first time. He said: I said: Glory be to Allah, who are these two? They said to me: Proceed, proceed. So I proceeded with them, and we came upon a man lying on his back with another standing over him with an iron hook, coming to one side of his face, tearing his cheek to his nape and his nostril to his nape and his eye to his nape. He said: Then he turned to the other side and did to it as he did to the first side, and he did not finish that side until the first became sound as it was, then he returned and did to him as he did the first time. He said: I said: Glory be to Allah, who are these two? They said to me: Proceed, proceed. He said: So we proceeded and came upon what resembled the build of an oven. Awf said: And I think he said: And in it were noise and voices. He said: I looked, and in it were naked men and women, and flames came to them from beneath them, and when that flame reached them they clamored. He said: I said: Who are these? They said to me: Proceed, proceed. He said: So we proceeded and came upon a river, I thought he said: Red like blood, and in the river was a man swimming, then that man who had gathered stones came and opened his mouth for him and fed him stone after stone. He said: He went and swam as he swam, then returned to him, and whenever he returned to him he opened his mouth and fed him a stone. He said: I said: What is this? They said to me: Proceed, proceed. So we proceeded and came upon a man of hateful appearance, the most hateful you see a man in appearance, and he was at a fire of his kindling it and going around it. He said: I said to them: What is this? They said to me: Proceed, proceed. He said: So we proceeded and came upon a green meadow with every blossom of spring in it. He said: And in the midst of the meadow was a tall man standing, I could hardly see his head for its height in the sky, and around the man were the most and finest boys I had ever seen. He said: I said to them: What is this and who are these? They said to me: Proceed, proceed. He said: So we proceeded and ended at a great tree, I never saw a tree greater nor finer. He said: They said to me: Climb in it. So we climbed in it, and I ended at a city built of bricks of gold and bricks of silver. We came to the gate of the city and sought opening, and it was opened for us, and we entered, and we met in it men half of whose creation was as the finest you see, and half as the ugliest you see. He said: They said to them: Go and fall into that river, and there was a small river lying across flowing as if it were pure milk in whiteness. He said: They went and fell into it, then returned to us with that evil gone from them, having become in the finest form. He said: They said to me: This is the Garden of Eden, and that is your dwelling. He said: While my sight went upward, there was a palace like the white cloud. They said to me: That is your dwelling. He said: I said to them: May Allah bless you, leave me to enter it. They said to me: Now no, but you will enter it. He said: I have seen wonders since tonight, so what is this I saw? They said to me: We shall inform you. As for the first man you came upon whose head is crushed with stone, he is a man who takes the Quran and rejects it and sleeps through the prescribed prayers. As for the man you came upon whose cheek is torn to his nape and his eye to his nape and his nostril to his nape, he is the man who goes out from his house and tells a lie reaching the horizons. As for the naked men and women in the build like the oven, they are the adulterers and adulteresses. As for the man swimming in the river and fed stones, he is the eater of usury. As for the hateful-looking man at the fire kindling it, he is Malik keeper of Hell. As for the tall man you saw in the meadow, he is Ibrahim peace be upon him. As for the boys around him, every newborn who died upon the fitrah. He said: Some Muslims said: O Messenger of Allah, and the children of the polytheists? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And the children of the polytheists. As for the people half of them fine and half ugly, they mixed a righteous deed with another evil, so Allah overlooked them."
"20355","I heard from Abbad ibn Abbad informing of it from Awf from Abu Raja from Samurah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: So the stone rolled here. My father said: I kept marveling at the eloquence of Abbad."
"20356","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he called the cupper, and he brought him horns and attached them to him. Affan once said: With a horn. Then he conditioned him with a blade. A Bedouin of Banu Fazarah, one of Banu Jadhimah, entered, and when he saw him cupped, having no acquaintance with cupping nor knowing it, he said: What is this, O Messenger of Allah, why do you let this one cut your skin? He said: This is cupping. He said: What is cupping? He said: This is among the best with which people treat."
"20357","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Sawadah narrated to me, he said: I heard Samurah ibn Jundub say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the call of Bilal deceive you, for in his sight is poorness, nor the whiteness seen at the top of predawn."
"20358","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb and Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, they said: Dawud narrated to us from Abu Qazah from al-Asqa ibn al-Asla from Samurah ibn Jundub from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whatever is below the ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire."
"20359","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us from Said from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sam is the father of the Arabs, and Ham is the father of the Abyssinians, and Yafith is the father of the Romans."
"20360","My father said, and Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Qatadah, he said: And al-Hasan narrated from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Sam is the father of the Arabs, and Yafith is the father of the Romans, and Ham is the father of the Abyssinians."
"20361","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Awf narrated to us from Abu Raja from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw on the night I was taken up a man swimming in a river and fed stones. I asked: What is this? It was said to me: The eater of usury."
"20362","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sallam ibn Abi Muti narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lineage is wealth, and nobility is piety."
"20363","Yunus ibn Muhammad and Husayn narrated to us, they said: Shayban narrated to us from Qatadah, and I heard Abu Nadrah narrating from Samurah ibn Jundub, that he heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among them are those whom the Fire takes to their ankles, and among them are those whom the Fire takes to their knees, and among them are those whom the Fire takes to their waists, and among them are those whom the Fire takes to their collarbones."
"20364","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us from Shubah from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah, and he did not hear it from him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we mutilate him."
"20365","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilabah from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear of your garments the white, and shroud in them your dead."
"20366","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Abd al-Malik from Zayd ibn Uqbah al-Fazari, he said: I entered upon al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf and said: May Allah set right the commander, shall I not narrate to you a hadith Samurah ibn Jundub narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. He said: I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begging is a scratch with which a man scratches his face. Whoever wishes keeps his face, and whoever wishes leaves, except that a man asks one in authority or asks in a matter he must."
"20367","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us from Mansur from Hilal ibn Yasaf from Rabi ibn Umaylah from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved speech to Allah Blessed and Exalted is four: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and Glory be to Allah, and Praise be to Allah. It does not harm you with which of them you begin."
"20368","Do not name your boy Yasar nor Rabah nor Najih nor Aflah, for you say: Is he there, and he is not, and he says: No. They are only four, do not add to me."
"20369","Rawh narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu Nadrah from Samurah ibn Jundub from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Among them are those whom the Fire takes to their knees, and among them are those whom it takes to their waists, and among them are those whom it takes to their collarbones."
"20370","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from al-Hasan from Samurah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever finds his goods with a bankrupt in their essence, he has more right to them."
"20371","And from Samurah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The dead is punished for what is wailed over him."
"20372","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from al-Hasan from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to be moderate in sitting and not to crouch."
"20373","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Attend Friday and draw near the imam, for a man keeps lagging from Friday until he lags from Paradise, though he is of its people."
"20374","Rawh narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us from al-Hasan from Samurah ibn Jundub from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever prays the dawn prayer is in the protection of Allah, so do not betray Allah Blessed and Exalted in His protection."
"20375","Rawh narrated to us from his book, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us from Qatadah, he said: Al-Hasan narrated from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sam is the father of the Arabs, and Yafith is the father of the Romans, and Ham is the father of the Abyssinians. And Rawh said in Baghdad from his memory: The children of Nuh are three: Sam and Ham and Yafith."
"20376","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Imran narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to propose over the proposal of his brother or to buy over his sale."
"20377","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two guardians marry, she belongs to the first, and when two guardians sell, the sale belongs to the first."
"20378","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from al-Hasan from Samurah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When Hawwa became pregnant, Iblis circled her, and no child lived for her. He said: Name him Abd al-Harith, for he will live. So they named him Abd al-Harith and he lived, and that was from the inspiration of Satan and his command."
"20379","Abdullah said: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting, and my strongest thought is that I heard it from him, he said: Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting, and I did not hear it from him: Qatadah narrated to us from Yahya ibn Malik from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Attend remembrance and draw near the imam, for a man keeps distancing until he is delayed in Paradise, though he enters it."
"20380","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to me from Matar from al-Hasan from Samurah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the caravans until they reach the markets, or a townsman selling for a Bedouin."
"20381","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever performs ablution, then with it and excellent, and whoever bathes, that is better."
"20382","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from al-Hasan from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman is married to two husbands, she belongs to the first of them, and when a sale is sold to two men, it belongs to the first of them."
"20383","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from al-Hasan from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we kill him, and whoever mutilates him, we mutilate him."
"20384","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us from Yunus from al-Hasan from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is near that Allah Almighty will fill your hands from the non-Arabs, then they will be lions who do not flee, killing your fighters and eating your spoils."
"20385","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Ismail meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, he said: I heard al-Shabi narrating from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed dawn and said: Is anyone here of Banu so-and-so? They said: Yes. He said: Your companion is detained at the gate of Paradise for a debt upon him."
"20386","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we kill him, and whoever mutilates him, we mutilate him."
"20387","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Hilal ibn Yasaf from Samurah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When I narrate to you a hadith, do not add to it. And he said: Four are among the finest speech, and they are from the Quran. It does not harm you with which of them you begin: Glory be to Allah, and Praise be to Allah, and There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest."
"20388","Then he said: Do not name your boy Aflah nor Najih nor Rabah nor Yasar."
"20389","Affan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us from al-Hasan from Samurah, he said: When he said takbir he paused a little, and when he finished reciting the chapter he paused a little. Imran ibn Husayn objected to him for that, so they wrote to Ubayy ibn Kab, and Ubayy wrote confirming him."
"20390","Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of the house has more right to the house."
"20391","And from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The middle prayer is the Asr prayer."
"20392","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever encloses a wall around land, it belongs to him."
"20393","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand is liable for what it takes until it renders it."
"20394","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we kill him, and whoever mutilates him, we mutilate him."
"20395","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With the boy is his aqiqah, slaughtered for him on his seventh day, and he is named and his head shaved."
"20396","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Thabit meaning Abu Zayd narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, mentioning that the one who narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted nabidh after he forbade it is Mundhir Abu Hassan, mentioning it from Samurah ibn Jundub. And he used to say: Whoever opposes al-Hajjaj has opposed."
"20397","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: While we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a bowl with tharid was brought. He said: He ate and the people ate, and they kept passing it around until near noon, each group eating then rising, and a group coming and taking it in turn. He said: A man said to him: Was it supplied with food? He said: As for from the earth, no, unless it was supplied from heaven."
"20398","Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us from al-Hasan, he said: A man came to him and said: A slave of his fled, and he vowed if he gained power over him to cut his hand. Al-Hasan said: Samurah narrated to us, he said: Seldom did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preach a sermon except he commanded charity in it and forbade mutilation in it."
"20399","Hushaym narrated to us, Shubah and others informed us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we kill him, and whoever mutilates him, we mutilate him."
"20400","Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Rukayn narrating from his father from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade naming your slaves four names: Aflah and Yasar and Nafi and Rabah."
"20401","Ishaq narrated to us, Saeed narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every boy is pledged for his aqiqah; it is slaughtered for him on the seventh day, his head is shaved, and he is named."
"20402","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to this whiteness; let your living wear it and shroud your dead in it, for it is among the best of your garments."
"20403","Amr ibn al-Haytham Abu Qatan narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two guardians marry off a woman, she belongs to the first of the two; and when a man sells a sale to two men, it belongs to the first of the two."
"20404","Ismail narrated to us, Saeed narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sellers have the choice so long as they have not separated."
"20405","Ismail narrated to us, Saeed narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling animal for animal on credit."
"20406","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Nuaim ibn Abi Hind, from Ibn Samurah ibn Jundub, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills, to him belongs the spoils taken from the slain."
"20407","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill the old men of the polytheists and spare their young. Abdullah said: I asked my father about the explanation of this hadith, Kill the old men of the polytheists; he said: He means the old man hardly ever accepts Islam, while the young man, that is, he may accept Islam, as if he is closer to Islam than the old man. He said: Al-sharkh means the youth."
"20408","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Saeed ibn Ubaid ibn Zaid ibn Uqbah, from his father, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When property is stolen from a man or property of his is lost, and he finds it intact in the hand of a man, he has more right to it, and the buyer reclaims the price from the seller."
"20409","Ismail narrated to us, from Saeed, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of the house has more right to the house."
"20410","Zakariya ibn Abi Zakariya narrated to us, Hushaim narrated to us, from Musa ibn al-Saib, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man has more right to his very property wherever he recognizes it, and the buyer pursues his seller."
"20411","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sawadah narrated to me, from his father, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let neither the adhan of Bilal nor this whiteness of the morning pillar deceive you, until it spreads wide."
"20412","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Shubah, Maabad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Zaid ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Jumuah: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"20413","Rawh narrated to us, Saeed narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab informed us, Saeed informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The Dajjal will come forth, and he is blind in the left eye, over it a thick growth; he will heal the blind and the leper and give life to the dead, and he will say to the people: I am your lord. Whoever says: You are my lord, he has been tempted; and whoever says: My Lord is Allah, until he dies, he has been protected from his trial, with no trial after it against him and no punishment. He will remain on earth as long as Allah wills, then Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon them both, will come from the direction of the west, confirming Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and following his religion, and he will kill the Dajjal. Then it is only the establishment of the Hour."
"20414","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umra, a lifetime grant of property, is valid for its recipients."
"20415","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the day of Hunayn was a rainy day, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his caller, who called out: Prayer in the dwellings."
"20416","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Sufyan, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, from Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Wear white garments, for they are purer and better, and shroud your dead in them."
"20417","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Saeed, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The middle prayer is the Asr prayer."
"20418","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, Ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The hand is liable for what it took until it delivers it. Then al-Hasan forgot afterwards and said: He does not guarantee."
"20419","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, from Amir, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr one day, then said: Is there anyone here from Banu Fulan, twice. A man said: Here he is. It is as if I hear the voice of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Your companion has been detained at the gate of Paradise because of a debt that was upon him."
"20420","Waki narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Sawadah ibn Hanzalah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let neither the adhan of Bilal nor the elongated dawn prevent you from your sahur; rather it is the dawn spreading across the horizon."
"20421","Waki narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Qudamah ibn Wabarah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever misses Jumuah, let him give charity of a dinar or half a dinar."
"20422","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Aswad ibn Qais al-Abdi, from Thalabah ibn Abbad, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer during an eclipse, and we did not hear any sound from him."
"20423","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, and Abu Nuaim narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Maabad ibn Khalid, from Zaid ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"20424","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Husayn, meaning al-Muallim, informed us, from Abdullah ibn Buraidah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the mother of Fulan, who died in childbirth, and he stood at her middle."
"20425","Yazid informed us, Shubah informed us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever narrates a hadith from me while deeming it a lie is one of the liars."
"20426","Muhammad ibn Ubaid narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Maabad ibn Khalid, from Zaid, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Jumuah: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"20427","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, he said: I heard Abu Raja al-Utaridi narrating from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the morning prayer, he turned to us with his face and said: Did any of you see a dream last night. If anyone had seen a dream that night, he would relate it to him, and he would say concerning it whatever Allah willed him to say. One day he asked us and said: Did any of you see a dream last night. He said: We said: No. He said: But I saw two men who came to me, took me by my hands, and brought me out to an open land, or a level land. They passed with me by a man, with another man standing over his head holding an iron hook; he puts it into his cheek and tears it until it reaches the back of his neck, then takes it out and puts it into his other side, while this side heals; he keeps doing that to him. I said: What is this. They said: Go on. So I went on with them, and there was a man lying on his back with another man standing holding a stone or a rock, crushing his head with it; the stone rolls away, and when he goes to take it, his head returns as it was, and he does the same again. I said: What is this. They said to me: Go on. So I went on with them, and there was a house built like the building of an oven, its top narrow and its bottom wide, with fire kindled beneath it; in it were naked men and women. When it flared they rose until they almost came out, and when it died down they returned into it. I said: What is this. They said to me: Go on. So I went on, and there was a river of blood in which was a man, and on the bank of the river a man with stones before him; the man in the river comes forward, and when he draws near to come out, he throws a stone into his mouth and he returns to his place; he keeps doing that to him. I said: What is this. They said: Go on. So I went on, and there was a green garden in which was a great tree, and at its root an old man with children around him, and near him a man with fire before him, stirring it and kindling it. They took me up the tree and admitted me into a house, never had I seen a house better than it; in it were old and young men, and women and children. Then they brought me out of it and took me up the tree and admitted me into a house better and more excellent than it, in it old and young men. I said to them: You have taken me around tonight, so tell me about what I saw. They said: Yes. As for the first man you saw, he is a liar who tells a lie that is carried from him across the horizons; what you saw will be done to him until the Day of Resurrection, then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will do with him what He wills. As for the man you saw lying down, he is a man to whom Allah, Blessed and Exalted, gave the Quran, but he slept away from it at night and did not act upon what is in it by day; what you saw will be done to him until the Day of Resurrection. As for those you saw in the oven, they are the adulterers. As for the one you saw in the river, that is the eater of usury. As for the old man you saw at the root of the tree, that is Ibrahim, peace be upon him; as for the children you saw, they are the children of mankind; as for the man you saw kindling the fire and stirring it, that is Malik, keeper of the Fire, and that is the Fire. As for the house you entered first, it is the house of the generality of the believers; as for the other house, it is the house of the martyrs. And I am Jibril and this is Mikail. Then they said to me: Raise your head. So I raised my head, and there it was like the appearance of a cloud. They said to me: And that is your house. I said to them: Let me enter my house. They said to me: There remains for you deeds you have not yet completed; if you completed them, you would enter your house."
"20428","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Humaid al-Tawil, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to keep two pauses: a pause when he opened the prayer, and a pause when he finished the second surah before bowing. That was mentioned to Imran ibn Husayn, who said: Samurah has lied. So he wrote about that to Madinah, to Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: Samurah has told the truth."
"20429","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, raising it, he said: Whoever owns a blood relative, he is free."
"20430","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Qazaah, from al-Asqa ibn al-Asla, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever is below the ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire."
"20431","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard al-Muhallab preaching, he said: Samurah ibn Jundub said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not pray when the sun rises nor when it sets, for it rises between the two horns of Satan and sets between the two horns of Satan."
"20432","Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: Rain befell us while we were with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he called out: Prayer in the dwellings."
"20433","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Among the best of what people treat themselves with is cupping."
"20434","Yahya ibn Abi Bukair narrated to us, he said: Zuhair ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umair narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr narrated to me, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he called a cupper and ordered him to cup him. He brought out cupping vessels of his made of horns and fastened them to him, then lanced him with the edge of a blade and poured the blood into a vessel beside him. A man from Banu Fazarah entered upon him and said: What is this, O Messenger of Allah; why do you let this man have your skin to cut it. He said: Then I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This is cupping. He said: And what is cupping. He said: It is among the best of what people treat themselves with."
"20435","Al-Ashyab narrated to us, Shaiban narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr al-Anbari, and he mentioned something like the hadith of Zuhair."
"20436","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Dawud narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, thereby and excellent; and whoever bathes, that is better."
"20437","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Dawud narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse one another with the curse of Allah, nor with His anger, nor with the Fire."
"20438","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, he said: Ali ibn Husayn said to me: The name of Jibril, peace be upon him, is Abdullah, and the name of Mikail, peace be upon him, is Ubaidullah."
"20439","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, thereby and excellent; and whoever bathes, bathing is better."
"20440","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Qais narrated to us, Thalabah ibn Abbad al-Abdi of the people of Basrah narrated to us, he said: One day I attended a sermon of Samurah ibn Jundub, and he mentioned in his sermon a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: While I and a boy of the Ansar were shooting at two targets of ours in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until when the sun, to the eye of the beholder, was a spear-length or two or three up, it darkened until it became as if it were a tannumah plant. He said: One of us said to his companion: Come with us to the mosque, for by Allah the affair of this sun will surely bring about a new matter to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning his ummah. He said: We hastened to the mosque, and there he was out in the open. He said: We met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as he came out to the people; he went forward and led us standing as long as he ever stood with us in any prayer, we hearing no sound from him. Then he bowed as long as he ever bowed with us in any prayer, we hearing no sound from him. Then he did the same in the second rakah, and his sitting in the second rakah coincided with the clearing of the sun. Zuhair said, I think he said: Then he gave salam, praised Allah and extolled Him, and testified that he is His slave and His Messenger. Then he said: O people, I ask you by Allah: if you know that I fell short in anything of conveying the messages of my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, you would have told me that. I have conveyed the messages of my Lord as they ought to be conveyed; and if you know that I conveyed the messages of my Lord, you would have told me that. He said: Men stood and said: We testify that you have conveyed the messages of your Lord, advised your ummah, and discharged what was upon you. Then they fell silent. Then he said: To proceed: Some men claim that the eclipse of this sun and the eclipse of this moon and the departure of these stars from their rising places is due to the death of great men among the people of the earth, and they have lied; rather they are signs among the signs of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, by which He admonishes His servants, to see who among them will newly repent. By Allah, since I stood to pray I have seen what you will meet in the affair of your world and your Hereafter. By Allah, the Hour will not come until thirty liars come forth, the last of them the one-eyed Dajjal, his left eye wiped as if it were the eye of Abu Yahya, referring to an old man then among the Ansar between him and the chamber of Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her. When he comes forth, or he said: whenever he comes forth, he will claim that he is Allah. Whoever believes in him, affirms him, and follows him, no past righteous deed of his will benefit him; and whoever disbelieves in him and denies him will not be punished for any of his deeds. And Hasan al-Ashyab said: for any evil of his past deeds. He will prevail, or he said: he will soon prevail, over the whole earth except the Sanctuary and Bayt al-Maqdis. He will besiege the believers in Bayt al-Maqdis, and they will be shaken with a severe shaking. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will destroy him and his troops, until the trunk of the wall, or he said: the root of the wall, and Hasan al-Ashyab said: and the root of the tree, will call out, or he said: will say: O believer, or he said: O Muslim, this is a Jew, or he said: this is a disbeliever, come and kill him. He said: That will not be so until you see matters whose gravity grows in yourselves, and you ask among yourselves whether your Prophet mentioned any mention of them to you, and until mountains shift from their stations. Then after that comes the seizure. He said: Then I attended a sermon of Samurah in which he mentioned this hadith, and he did not put a word forward nor put it back from its place."
"20441","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran was sent down upon seven modes."
"20442","Umar ibn Sad Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qais, from Thalabah ibn Abbad, from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached when the sun eclipsed and said: To proceed."
"20443","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: You are about to have Allah, Blessed and Exalted, fill your hands with the non-Arabs, and Affan once said: with the foreigners; then they will be lions who do not flee, killing your fighters and eating your war booty."
"20444","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hisham, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sellers have the choice so long as they have not separated."
"20445","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The neighbor has more right to the vicinity, or to the house."
"20446","Suraij ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Thalabah, from Makhul, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to take mosques in our quarters, and commanded us to clean them."
"20447","Al-Fadl ibn Dukain narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Habib, from Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white garments, for they are purer and better, and shroud your dead in them."
"20448","Al-Hasan ibn Yahya of the people of Marw and Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Wiqa ibn Iyas, from Ali ibn Rabiah, from Samurah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and preached, and he forbade dubba gourds and muzaffat pitch-coated vessels."
"20449","Abdullah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Jamil narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us the like of it. Khalaf ibn Hisham and Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qais, from Thalabah, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"20450","He narrated to us. [Source text truncated]"
"20451","Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Every boy is pledged for his aqiqah; it is slaughtered for him on his seventh day, harm is removed from him, and he is named."
"20452","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sellers have the choice so long as they have not separated, and each of them takes what he accepts of the sale."
"20453","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Qais narrated to us, from Thalabah ibn Abbad, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: One day he stood preaching and mentioned in his sermon a hadith. He said: While I and a boy of the Ansar were shooting at two targets of ours in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the sun rose until, to the eye of the beholder, it was a spear-length or two, and he drove the hadith on. Then he said: To proceed. And he said: Then he closed the tips of his fingers. Then he said, or he stood, I doubt, another time, and I have memorized what he said. He said: He did not put a word forward from its station nor delay anything. Abu Awanah said: While I and a boy of the Ansar. He also said: Then it darkened until it became so. Abu Awanah said: Zool, but it is Zool that is more correct."
"20454","Khalaf ibn Hisham and Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qais, from Thalabah, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"20455","Ali narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade celibate renunciation of marriage."
"20456","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every boy is pledged for his aqiqah; it is slaughtered on his seventh day, his head is shaved, and he is stained with its blood."
"20457","Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, except that he said: And he is named. Hammam said in his hadith, and we reviewed him: And he is stained with blood. Hammam said: Qatadah used to describe the blood, saying: When the aqiqah is slaughtered, a tuft of wool is taken and held to the jugular veins of the slaughtered animal, then placed on the fontanel of the boy until, when it flows, his head is washed, then he is shaved afterwards."
"20458","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The neighbor of the house has more right to the house than another."
"20459","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulaiman al-Taimi narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl containing tharid, and they took turns at it from morning until noon, some people rising and others sitting. A man said to him: Was it replenished. He said: At what do you wonder; it was replenished only from here, and he pointed to the sky."
"20460","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever kills his slave, we kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we mutilate him."
"20461","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Abu Umayyah, a shaykh of his: Al-Hasan narrated to us, from Samurah, he said: And whoever castrates his slave, we castrate him."
"20462","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, and Abu Dawud informed us, Hisham informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The neighbor of the house has more right to the house."
"20463","Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit and al-Hakam, from Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white garments, for they are better and purer, and shroud your dead in them."
"20464","Yazid narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, from Ishaq ibn Thalabah, from Makhul, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should take from his brothers captive to kill him."
"20465","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Saeed ibn Zaid ibn Uqbah, from his father, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes upon his very goods has more right to them, and his companion pursues whoever bought them from him. Yazid once said: Whoever finds his goods."
"20466","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, he said: I heard Sawadah al-Qushairi narrating from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Let neither the adhan of Bilal nor this elongated dawn deceive you; rather it is the spreading dawn. And he gestured with his hand thus, and Yazid gestured with his right hand."
"20467","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever owns a mahram blood relative, he is freed."
"20468","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Awf informed us, and Hawdhah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, a shaykh from Bakr ibn Wail in a qasamah gathering narrated to us, he said: I entered upon Samurah while he was being cupped, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Among the best of your remedies is cupping."
"20469","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two guardians marry off a woman, she belongs to the first of the two; and when a man sells a sale to two men, it belongs to the first of the two."
"20470","Rawh narrated to us, Saeed narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among them is one whom the Fire takes up to his knees, among them one whom the Fire takes up to his waist, and among them one whom the Fire takes up to his collarbone."
"20471","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdillah and Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever woman two guardians marry off, she belongs to the first of the two; and whatever man sells a sale to two men, it belongs to the first of the two."
"20472","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us, and Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umair narrated to us, from Husayn, a man of Banu Fazarah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: A bedouin came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was preaching and cut off his sermon, saying: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the dabb lizard. He said: A nation transformed from Banu Israil, and I do not know which beasts were transformed."
"20473","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shaiban narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Husayn ibn Qabisah al-Fazari, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: A bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
"20474","Sulaiman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his caller, who called out on a rainy day: Prayer in the dwellings."
"20475","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umair narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being cupped with a horn and lanced with the edge of a knife. A man from Shamkh entered and said to him: Why do you let your back or your neck be at the mercy of this man, doing with it what I see. He said: This is cupping, and it is among the best of what you treat yourselves with."
"20476","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Buraidah narrated to us, that he heard Samurah ibn Jundub saying: What prevents me from speaking much of what I used to hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is that here are those more numerous than I, and that night I was a boy, yet I used to memorize what I heard from him. I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed over Umm Kab, who died in childbirth; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for prayer over her at her middle."
"20477","Yahya ibn Saeed and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Saeed narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever kills his slave, we kill him; and whoever mutilates him, we mutilate him. Yahya said: Then al-Hasan forgot afterwards and said: He is not killed for him."
"20478","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, Saeed ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade selling animal for animal on credit. Yahya said: Then al-Hasan forgot and said: When the two kinds differ, there is no harm."
"20479","Yahya narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Buraidah narrated to us, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a woman who died in childbirth, and he stood at her middle."
"20480","Waki narrated to us, Misar and Sufyan narrated to us, from Maabad ibn Khalid, from Zaid ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to recite in the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"20481","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white garments and shroud your dead in them, for they are purer and better."
"20482","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, from Zaid ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These begging questions are scratches with which one of you scratches his face. And Ibn Jafar said: wounds with which a man is wounded, except that he ask a ruler or in a matter from which there is no escape."
"20483","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qais, from Thalabah ibn Abbad, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed during an eclipse, and no sound was heard from him."
"20484","Waki narrated to us, he said: Shubah said, and al-Hakam narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever narrates a hadith while deeming it a lie is one of the liars."
"20485","Waki narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr and said: Is there anyone here from Banu Fulan, three times. A man said: I am. He said: Then he said: Your companion is detained from Paradise because of his debt."
"20486","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhail, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best speech after the Quran is four, and they are from the Quran; it will not harm you with which of them you begin: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great."
"20487","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Affan narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Layla. Affan said in his hadith: Al-Hakam informed us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever narrates a hadith from me while deeming it a lie is one of the liars. Affan also said: The great liars."
"20488","Waki narrated to us, Yazid, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us with a sermon but forbade us mutilation and commanded us charity."
"20489","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, he said: Samurah ibn Jundub said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do not pray when the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of a devil, nor when it sets, for it sets between the two horns of a devil."
"20490","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever owns a mahram blood relative, he is free."
"20491","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humaid, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to keep two silences: when he entered the prayer and when he finished the recitation. Imran ibn Husayn denied that, so they wrote to Ubayy ibn Kab asking him about that, and he wrote that Samurah had told the truth."
"20492","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Uthman ibn Sad the scribe informed us, he said: Ibn Sirin said to me: I made my sword after the sword of Samurah. And Samurah said: I made my sword after the sword of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was Hanafi."
"20493","Hushaim narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill the old men of the polytheists and spare their young."
"20494","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Shabi, from Saman ibn Mushannaj, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a funeral, and he said: Is there anyone here from Banu Fulan, saying it three times. A man stood, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What prevented you on the first two occasions from answering me. I did not call you out but for good: So-and-so, a man among them who died, is held back by his debt. He said: He said: I saw his family and those grieving for him pay on his behalf until none came demanding anything."
"20495","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Shabi, from Samurah, and he mentioned the hadith."
"20496","Abu Sufyan al-Mamari narrated to us, from Sufyan, from his father, from al-Shabi, from Saman ibn Mushannaj, from Samurah ibn Jundub, and he mentioned the hadith."
"20497","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaibah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from his father, from Saeed ibn Masruq, from al-Shabi, and he mentioned this hadith. So I narrated it to my father, and he said: I did not hear it from Waki."
"20498","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, and Rawh narrated to us, Saeed ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to this whiteness; your best men wear it. And Rawh said: Let your living wear it. And shroud your dead in it, for it is among the best of your garments."
"20499","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zaid narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, he said: Samurah said, and he mentioned it. And Affan mentioned from Wuhaib also, in which Abu al-Muhallab is absent."
"20500","Abdah narrated to us, Saeed narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling animal for animal on credit."
"20501","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever encloses a wall around a land, it is his."
"20502","'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, the like of it, except that he said: Whoever encloses."
"20503","Zakariyya ibn 'Adi narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah informed us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Husayn ibn Qabisah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: A bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was delivering the sermon, and interrupted his sermon, saying: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about lizards? He said: A community from the Children of Israel was transformed, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, knows best into which animals they were transformed."
"20504","'Abd al-Samad and 'Affan said, Hisham narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The two parties to a sale have the choice so long as they have not parted."
"20505","'Abd al-Samad and 'Affan said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, al-Ash'ath ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Jarmi informed us, from his father, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that a man said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw as if a bucket was let down from heaven, then Abu Bakr, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, came and took hold of its sides and drank from it a weak drink - 'Affan said: and in it is weakness - then 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, came and took hold of its sides and drank until he was fully satisfied, then 'Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, came and took hold of its sides and drank, then it was snatched from him and some of it splashed onto him."
"20506","'Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pause two pauses, when he entered the prayer and when he finished the recitation, and 'Imran ibn Husayn denied that, and they wrote to Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and he wrote to them that Samurah spoke the truth."
"20507","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Rabi' ibn 'Umaylah al-Fazari, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most beloved speech to Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, is four: There is no god but Allah, glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, and Allah is Most Great; it does not harm you with which of them you begin."
"20508","And do not name your boy Yasar, nor Rabah, nor Najih, nor Aflah, for you say: Is he there? And he is not there, so he says: No; they are only four, so do not add to me."
"20509","Isma'il narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: Samurah said: I memorized two pauses in the prayer, a pause when the imam says Allahu akbar until he recites, and a pause when he finishes reciting the Opening of the Book and a surah before bowing. He said: 'Imran ibn Husayn denied that against him, so they wrote to Ubayy about that, to Madinah. He said: So Samurah spoke the truth."
"20510","Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: It is imminent that Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, will fill your hands with the non-Arabs, then Allah will make them lions who do not flee, and they will kill your fighters and eat your booty."
"20511","Mu'ammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is imminent that Allah will fill your hands, then he mentioned the like of it."
"20512","'Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: You are about to have Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, fill your hands with the non-Arabs, then they will be lions who do not flee, and they will kill your fighters and eat your booty."
"20513","Hushaym informed us, Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, then he mentioned the like of it."
"20514","My father said, and Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated it to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"20515","'Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The neighbor has more right to his adjoining property."
"20516","'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The two parties to a sale have the choice so long as they have not parted, or each one of them takes what he is pleased with of the sale."
"20517","He narrated to us."
"20518","'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A life grant is permissible."
"20519","'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The middle prayer is the 'Asr prayer."
"20520","'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: Every child is pledged for his 'aqiqah, slaughtered on his seventh day, and shaved, and smeared with blood."
"20521","'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Bishr ibn Harb informed us, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said, I think it raised: Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it, and the next day at its time."
"20522","Yunus and Surayj said, Hammad narrated to us, from Bishr, he said: I heard Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said the like of it."
"20523","'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, then by it, and excellent it is; and whoever bathes, that is better."
"20524","'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the day of Hunayn was a rainy day, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered his caller: Prayer is in the dwellings."
"20525","'Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, the like of it, exactly."
"20526","'Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Qur'an came down in three readings. 'Affan once said: The Qur'an was sent down."
"20527","'Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When two men marry a woman, the first is more entitled; and when two men buy goods, the first is more entitled."
"20528","'Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling animals for animals on credit."
"20529","'Affan informed us, Shu'bah informed us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr informed me, he said: I heard Zayd ibn 'Uqbah, he said: I heard Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Begging is scratches with which a man scratches his face; whoever wishes may preserve his face, and whoever wishes may leave off, except that a man asks one in authority, or asks in a matter from which he finds no escape. He said: So I narrated it to al-Hajjaj, and he said: Ask me, for I am one in authority."
"20530","Hushaym informed us, Mansur and Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that when he used to pray with them he paused two pauses, when he opened the prayer, and when he said nor of those astray he also paused briefly; they denied that against him, so he wrote to Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and Ubayy wrote to them that the matter is as Samurah did."
"20531","'Affan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Yunus, he said: And when he finished reciting the surah."
"20532","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sallam ibn Abi Muti' narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Tha'labah ibn 'Abbad, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in prayer during the solar eclipse, two rak'ahs, in which we did not hear a voice from him."
"20533","Isma'il and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The two parties to a sale have the choice so long as they have not parted."
